   "severity": "advisory",
   "why_advisory": "48 rows / 5,034 instances on 16 of 19 targets (source-repo measurement 2026-09-11: 57/57 page-viewports, two identical runs, examined = 104 siblings each). The sibling corpus is every built page, never same-page-type targets, so no page type examines 0. Stays advisory: Foundation is a verbatim WordPress migration, so crossover on migrated bodies is the baseline projects 3 and 4 clear, not a check defect. Re-measure on BSUK's own corpus before promoting."
  },
  {
   "id": "first-person-brand-voice",
   "family": "COPY",
   "enforced": "judgment",
   "why": "a regex for we/our passes on third-person text that merely mentions us; the distinction is authorial stance, which has no mechanical decision procedure",
   "pack": "rules/copy.md"
  },
  {
   "id": "work-on-foundation-not-main",
   "family": "GATE",
   "enforced": "judgment",
   "why": "governs the operator's git behaviour before any artifact exists; a test can assert the branch name but not that nothing was pushed, and BSUK has no remote to observe",
   "pack": "rules/deploy.md"
  },
  {
   "id": "commit-after-build-never-push",
   "family": "GATE",
   "enforced": "judgment",
   "pack": "rules/deploy.md",
   "why": "a test could assert a clean working tree, but not that the work was finished, and asserting the former would pass on an empty commit; the 'never push' half has no observable at all while the repo has no remote"
  },
  {
   "id": "recommend-plus-why",
